# Noesis Status Check

Run these commands and report results concisely:

```bash
# Bridge
ls {{ claude_code_bridge_dir }}/inbox/ 2>/dev/null
tail -3 {{ claude_code_bridge_dir }}/channel.jsonl 2>/dev/null

# Health
hermes status 2>&1 | head -20

# Repos
git -C ~/projects/noesis-agent-stack status --short 2>/dev/null | head
git -C ~/projects/noesis-ansible status --short 2>/dev/null | head

# Crons
hermes cron list 2>&1 | grep -c "\[active\]" || true
```

Report format:

```
Agent: [healthy/down]
Bridge: X pending inbox, Y unread channel
Repos: [clean/dirty] agent-stack, [clean/dirty] ansible
Crons: X active
Last activity: [from channel tail]
```
